  "_source": "Hand-curated and bundled with this Play. Not fetched, not generated, not derived from any ranking list or third-party service; every row was written by a person and can be read, argued with and edited in this file.",
  "_note": "Not exhaustive, and deliberately not clever. It maps registrable domains only, so every subdomain of a listed domain inherits its category and nothing else is inferred. A domain that is not in this list is reported as `uncategorised` and counted as such; it is never guessed at from its name, its TLD or its neighbours. Three known limits are stated rather than hidden. (1) There is no `search` category and portal domains are excluded on purpose: google.com, yahoo.com and their kin are simultaneously search, mail, video, documents and storage, so categorising the registrable domain would be a lie in four directions, and a pure search engine such as duckduckgo.com has no category here to be put in. All of them land in `uncategorised`, which is the honest answer for a page whose subject the domain does not reveal. (2) Rolling up to the registrable domain merges genuinely different products: docs.aws.amazon.com counts as amazon.com and therefore as `shopping`, and learn.microsoft.com counts as microsoft.com. (3) `docs` means reference material and the documents you work in, which includes issue trackers and note tools; `local` is a machine talking to itself and is decided in code from the host, not from this list, so the one row here is only a convenience.",
